    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when more than 80 owners have already been created today, the owner response carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`, otherwise `false`.\n\nI kept structural impact minimal by reusing the existing `namesakeCount` transient pattern and the daily-count helper already in scope, touching three files with single small additions:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no change to `OwnerMapper`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean bulkSignupWarning` with a plain getter/setter, mirroring the adjacent `namesakeCount` field. New, self-contained accessors (CC 1) rather than growing any existing method.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one straight-line statement (no new branch, so the method's cyclomatic complexity is unchanged) that reuses the already-fetched `owners` collection and the existing `DailyRegistrations.countOn` helper:\n   ```java\n   owner.setBulkSignupWarning(DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, java.time.LocalDate.now()) > 80);\n   ```\n\nThe value is computed at create time against the count of owners already registered today (matching \"already been created today\"), stored on the managed entity, and read back through the mapper on `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 exactly the path the acceptance test exercises. A freshly created owner under the threshold serializes `false`.",
